# AI cost and attribution (I2 / I3)

Guide: `docs/ai-platform/03-cost-guards.md`.

## Spend gate

1. **API**: `assertAiSpendAllowed` (or equivalent) **before** enqueue — fast fail UX.
2. **Worker controller**: assert again — authoritative.
3. Run the model via `runAiRequest`.
4. **`recordSpendUsage` only after success.** Ledger write failures must not fail a completed job (errors swallowed after success).

If AI is disabled: failed job + `AiDisabledError` (do not call the model).

## Attribution

| Caller | `requestedBy` | Tenant ledger | User ledger | Role meters |
|--------|---------------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| Interactive UI | Firebase UID | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| System / nightly | `"system"` or empty | Yes | No | No |

Use `isAttributableAiUserId` semantics — do not attribute system jobs to a fake user.

## Limits

- Tenant: `tenant.aiLimits` / spend collections under `tenants/{tenantId}/…`
- Roles: `aiSpendLimits` on role catalog entries
- Permissions gate features (`ai.chat.run`, etc.)

## Do not

- Call Vertex outside the controller “to save a round trip”
- Record spend on failed model calls
- Skip API-side guard because the worker will check

## Enforcement

- Spend unit tests in `@repo/ai-engine`
- API route tests for 403 spend limits
- Debugger: `/debugger/ai-jobs`

